qemu-3dfx makes SDL2 a hard requirement of the whole build ("Featuring
qemu-3dfx required SDL2") because upstream's only 3D UI provider lives in
ui/sdl2.c. Ours does not: patch 30 puts the eleven entry points behind a
vtable any frontend can register, and the player registers the embed
library's window-less provider (embed/embedfx.c). Nothing 2ksbox ships
opens a QEMU window, so scripts/configure-qemu.sh passes --disable-sdl and
this error is the only thing standing in the way (2026-09-07).

The pass-through devices themselves are unaffected: hw/3dfx and hw/mesa are
built unconditionally (meson.build's subdir() calls are not gated on SDL),
and their native context backend is GLX, not SDL.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -1561,7 +1561,6 @@
     error('sdl-image required, but SDL was @0@'.format(
           get_option('sdl').disabled() ? 'disabled' : 'not found'))
   endif
-  error('Featuring qemu-3dfx required SDL2')
   sdl_image = not_found
 endif
 
